# Error Handling Patterns

1. When to Throw vs Log
### Scenario	Action
  - Public action/mutation	throw new ConvexError() - error reaches frontend
  - Internal action (critical)	throw new ConvexError() - propagates to caller
  - Internal action (non-critical)	console.warn() + return - graceful degradation
  - Webhook handlers	throw new ConvexError() for critical, return for non-critical

2. ConvexError vs Error
  - ConvexError: All public mutations/actions (provides structured { code, message })
  - Error: Never use in Convex functions - always use ConvexError

3. Logging Levels
### Level	Use Case
  - console.error()	Actual failures that need investigation
  - console.warn()	Recoverable issues, rate limits, missing optional data
  - console.log()	Removed - use structured logging instead

4. Error Codes
Backend error codes are defined in the `errors/constants.ts` file in the backend @packages/backend/convex/errors/constants.ts.